<title>FRANCE: AXA-UAP Q1 1997 revenues up 11 pct.</title>
<headline>AXA-UAP Q1 1997 revenues up 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter 1997.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Total					   98,663    vs   88,921</p>
<p>    Life insurance				49,045    vs   42,569</p>
<p>     - Europe				     31,773    vs   29,363</p>
<p>     - North America			    11,389    vs    9,411</p>
<p>     - Asia Pacific				5,854    vs    3,750</p>
<p>     - Africa					   30    vs	 45</p>
<p>    Property and Casualty Insurance	 31,262    vs   30,538</p>
<p>     - Europe				     29,228    vs   28,699</p>
<p>     - North America				 781    vs	808</p>
<p>     - Asia Pacific				   81    vs	 70</p>
<p>     - Africa					  135    vs	216</p>
<p>     - Axa Global Risks			  1,037    vs	745</p>
<p>   Reinsurance				     5,487    vs    5,912</p>
<p>   Total insurance and reinsurance	  85,795    vs   79,019</p>
<p>   Financial services and holding firms   12,868    vs    9,902</p>
<p>     - Europe					2,458    vs    2,617</p>
<p>     - North America			    10,372    vs    7,253</p>
<p>     - Asia Pacific				   38    vs	 32</p>
<p>NOTE - French insurance company Axa-UAP said in a statement that consolidated revenues rose by 11 percent. On a constant currency and structural basis, consolidated revenues rose by 6.1 percent. Life insurance revenues were up 8.0 percent on a like- for-like basis against 15.2 percent on a percentage change basis. -- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
